<title>FRANCE: Lufthansa tops Europe long-haul 96 air cargo table.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa tops Europe long-haul 96 air cargo table.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lufthansa flew the most freight tonne-kilometres (FTKs) on long-haul routes among European carriers in 1996, figures from the Association of European Airlines (AEA) show.</p>
<p>The FTK measurement is derived by multiplying the weight of cargo carried by the distance flown.</p>
<p>FTKs (in millions) transported by AEA member airlines in 1996, with 1995 ranking in parentheses and percentage change on 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1 (1)   Lufthansa		5,354	  +2.4</p>
<p>    2 (2)   Air France	     4,510	  +5.0</p>
<p>    3 (3)   KLM			3,527	  +4.0</p>
<p>    4 (4)   British Airways	3,153	  +7.3</p>
<p>    5 (5)   Cargolux		 2,020	  +4.1</p>
<p>    6 (6)   Swissair		 1,509	  +8.7</p>
<p>    7 (7)   Alitalia		 1,366	  -1.0</p>
<p>    8 (8)   Iberia		     614	  +8.3</p>
<p>    9 (9)   SAS			  559	 +41.9</p>
<p>    10 (10) Sabena		     303	 -20.0</p>
<p>    11 (11) Finnair		    197	 +13.7</p>
<p>    12 (12) TAP			  151	 +12.9</p>
<p>    13 (13) Turkish Airlines	 111	 -12.2</p>
<p>    14 (15) Austrian Airlines	100	 +11.8</p>
<p>    15 (14) Aer Lingus		  95	  -4.6</p>
<p>    16 (16) Olympic Airways	   64	  +3.3</p>
<p>    17 (17) Icelandair		  33	  +24.1</p>
<p>    18 (19) Malev			 22	  +2.1</p>
<p>    19 (18) Balkan			17	  -24.0</p>
<p>    20 (20) CSA			   14	   -19.1</p>
<p>    Total AEA*			23,720	   +4.6</p>
<p>*Adria Airways, Air Malta, British Midland, Cyprus Airways, JAT and Luxair do not operate long-haul services.</p>
<p>    Total AEA**		     25,851</p>
<p>**All scheduled services  (including domestic)</p>
